[ti:Day 27]

[00:00.00]chit 例 Sally initialed the chit for the barman. 萨莉 为酒吧侍应生签了收据。
[00:05.54]prompt 例 The measure prompts the branch leaders to reconsider how they should manage their group members. 这项措施促使各分部领导重新 考虑如何管理下属。
[00:18.20]wield 例 Both China and Japan wield great influences in Asia's economic development. 中 国和日本都对亚洲的经济发展产生着极大的影 响。
[00:28.29]cafeteria 例 On the ocean side of the 105-meter tower is a cafeteria and a store. 在这座105米高的大 厦的临海一侧是一家自助餐厅和一家便利店。
[00:37.53]liable 例 As one of the stockholders of the company, she is liable to pay their debts. 作为公司的股东 之一，她有义务偿还债务。
[00:47.34]countertrade 例 Countertrade can be used to stimulate home industries or where raw materials are in short supply. 反向贸易可以用来促进国内产业或 者原材料短缺的产业。
[01:00.85]hosier 例 Six years ago, she set up her own business as a hosier. 五年前，她以袜类销售商的身份创建 了自己的企业。
[01:08.10]signify 例 The card signifles membership of the institution. 那张卡象征着该机构的会员身份。
[01:15.36]indisputably 例 They are indisputably one of the best teams in China in terms of flnancial investment. 毋庸置疑，他们是中国金融投资领域 的最佳团队之一。
[01:27.44]approach 例 You'll approach the task more confidently knowing that you're ready. 在你清楚你已经准备 好的情况下你会更有信心地着手处理这项任务。
[01:37.11]inquiry 例 I made a confldential inquiry into the recent business event. 我对最近发生的商业事件作了秘 密调查。
[01:45.64]impulse 例 Impulse is not the character of a successful person. 冲动不是成功人士该具备的品格。
[01:53.04]cost 例 We have to weigh the cost of the new system against the beneflts it will bring. 我们 必须权衡一下启用新系统所需的成本和它将带来 的效益。
[02:02.85]induction 例 His induction as a salesman transformed his life. 从事销售工作是他一生的转折点。
[02:10.24]simultaneously 例 Urbanisation should integrate migrant workers into the cities while simultaneously develop a modern agricultural sector. 城市化不 仅要把流动工人纳入城市，还要同时发展现代农 业体系。
[02:27.45]banking 例 People are starting to believe that the Chinese yuan is playing an increased role in international banking transactions. 人们开始觉 得中国的人民币在国际银行业务中扮演着越来越 重要的角色。
[02:43.23]lucrative 例 According to his long working experience, he thought the project a lucrative one. 根据多 年的从业经验，他认为这个项目是有利可图的。
[02:54.46]continuation 例 In a very real sense, post-war recession was the continuation of the war. 就真正意义上 来说，战后经济衰退就是战争的延续。
[03:04.98]clearing 例 Most senior financiers are willing to move some activity on to a clearing platform. 大多数 高级金融家都愿意把部分交易行为放到结算平台 上。
[03:16.22]zip 例 It's very cold outside, so you'd better zip up your jacket. 外面特别冷；你最好拉好上衣拉链。
[03:23.75]counterfeit 例 Counterfeit goods infringe customers' legal r ights. 伪造商品侵害了消费者的合法权益。
[03:32.00]authenticate 例 Science has long been used to help authenticate works of art. 人们很早就开始运用 科学来鉴别艺术品的真假。
[03:41.10]ferocious 例 In campaigns, he was a loyal friend and a ferocious opponent who believed the power of politics can change lives. 在竞选中，他是忠诚 的朋友和强悍的对手，相信政治的力量可以改变 许多人的生活。
[03:55.89]squander 例 A mechanism is being established to make it impossible for government officials to squander public money at their own will. 目前 正在建立一项机制来防止政府官员乱花公款。
[04:11.95]confusion 例 His speech flung the meeting into confusion. 他的发言使得会议陷入混乱。
[04:18.78]off-season 例 The off-season price for a standard room is about $50 a night. 标准间的淡季价格是每晚 50美元。
[04:27.59]convenance 例 Although it is a social convenance internationally, there're still some differences of opinions between countries. 虽然这是国际通 行的社交礼仪，但在不同国家也有不同的惯例。
[04:43.38]goodwill 例 If you think that the value of any of the businesses you have acquired has gone down, you can write off some or all of that goodwill. 如果你认为你所购买的企业贬值了，你可以撤销 该企业的部分或者全部营业权。
[04:59.87]shortfall 例 There is a great shortfall in the supply of senior medical talents. 高级医学人才缺口很大。
[05:09.26]archrival 例 Corporations make up Google's archrival Microsoft's traditional customer base. 企业客 户是谷歌的主要对手微软的传统客户群。
[05:20.63]fortunate 例 Do not speak of your happiness to one less fortunate than yourself. 不要向不如你幸运的人 讲述你的幸福。
[05:30.01]reinstate 例 She was reinstated as assistant to the general manager. 她又恢复总经理助理的职位 了。
[05:38.12]perspective 例 You can see yourself from a new perspective. 你可以从全新的角度去了解你自 己。
[05:45.09]decipher 例 She reluctantly got out the paper and pen in preparation for deciphering the words in the code. 她很不情愿地取出了纸笔，准备破解密码 内容。
[05:57.60]concede 例 They concede the financial industry's pay and bonus regime is under unprecedented strain. 他们承认，金融业的薪金和奖金体系正面 临前所未有的压力。
[06:09.68]thrive 例 If the business is to thrive, this is the only opportunity you can seize. 如果你想让你的企业 兴盛起来，这是你能抓住的唯一机会。
[06:19.21]arbitrate 例 An independent board is set up specially to arbitrate between management and the unions. 为了在资方与工会之间进行仲裁，已专门 成立了一个独立机构。
[06:31.30]amelioration 例 No other questions received as much attention or stimulated as many investigations and proposals for amelioration as this one. 再 没有其他问题像这个问题一样，受到如此多的注 意，引发如此多的调查和改良建议。
[06:48.50]urge 例 According to the treaty, France will help to urge the EU to relax restrictions on exporting high-tech products to China. 根据协议，法国 将帮忙力劝欧盟放松对出口中国的高科技产品的 限制。
[07:03.57]brainstorm 例 The new generation of market leaders will do more than just brainstorm their way to success. 下一代的市场领导人为了成功将会做得 更多，而不是仅仅用头脑风暴的方式。
[07:16.09]apprentice 例 You can't expect an apprentice to have the same dexterity as a master craftsman. 你不能 期望学徒做得像熟练的技工一样灵活。
[07:27.18]courier 例 The service works by aggregating capacity across local courier companies into a single web-service that retailers can use to speed up deliveries. 这项业务通过把当地各个快递公司 的运货能力聚集到一个网络服务，使零售商节省 了送货时间。
[07:45.95]avid 例 The international market has become increasingly avid about classical music in recent years. 近年来，国际市场对古典音乐越来 越感兴趣。
[07:58.03]slack 例 Don't be slack in your work. 干活不要马虎。
[08:02.15]forefront 例 We launched different actions to convince the consumers of the importance of this problem, especially at the forefront was the question linked with health and safety. 我们开 展了不同的活动以使消费者认识到这一问题的重 要性，尤其是涉及健康和安全的问题。
[08:23.62]declassify 例 Only recently has the Japanese government begun to acknowledge the case and to declassify historical records on it. 直到近期， 日本政府才开始承认该事件并解密其历史记录。
[08:39.12]let 例 He decided to let the larger room at a monthly rent of ￥1000. 他决定把较大的房间以 每月1000元的价格出租。
[08:46.66]perquisite 例 The perquisites of my job include health insurance and a performance bonus. 我这份工 作的额外津贴包括健康保险和绩效奖金。
[08:57.32]indefeasible 例 The appropriate rights of the staff are indefeasible. 员工的正当权利是不能取消的。
[09:05.71]customer 例 The customer will be reimbursed for any loss or damage. 顾客受到的一切损失或损害都将 得到赔偿。
[09:13.53]banner 例 Under the banner of peace, development and cooperation, the development of China has achieved great progress. 在和平、发展与合 作的目标指引下，中国已经取得了长足的发展。
[09:27.89]fertilise 例 One widely discussed idea, which the Royal Society's correspondents re-examined, was to fertilise the oceans with iron. 一个受到广泛讨 论并被皇家学会成员再次斟酌的观点是利用铁物 质对海洋施肥。
[09:43.96]secrecy 例 The meeting was arranged in secrecy. 那个 会议是秘密安排的。
[09:49.50]assume 例 We must assume him to be innocent until he is proven guilty. 在未证实他有罪之前，我们 就得假定他是清白的。
[09:57.47]fast-expanding 例 The development of gas trade has stepped into a fast-expanding period. 天然气贸易的发 展已经进入了高速扩张期。
[10:08.13]legacy 例 These records about production are his legacy to the factory. 这些关于生产的记录是他 留给工厂的东西。
[10:16.52]authorise 例 The company did not authorise the fifth business department to do chartering business. 公司并没有授权第五业务部门开展租赁 业务。
[10:28.46]resentful 例 He is resentful towards his employer. 他对 老板心怀不满。
